meta {
  name: Get Product Category by ID
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-categories/6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.n_children: eq 1
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Fetches the
  parent category created in "Create Product Category.bru" -- `n_children`
  is now `1` after the child was created, confirming nesting persisted.

  ## Subpath discovery (Phase 0 technique reused)
  `GET /product-categories/{id}/bogus_xyz` -- 400
  `{"errors":[{"name":"ValueError","description":"Field 'bogus_xyz' not
  found. Available fields: ['id','account_id','name','parent_id','path',
  'slug','order','n_children','created','modified']"}]}`. Unlike products,
  this raw field list matches the spec's `ProductCategoryGetOutputDto`
  exactly (no undocumented internal fields).

  Also confirmed: `GET /product-categories/{child_id}/parent` -- 200,
  returns the expanded parent object (a computed subpath, same as
  products' `categories`/`assets` subpaths -- not in the raw field list
  above but still valid).

  ## Identifier flexibility -- confirms Phase 0's product finding generalizes
  `GET /product-categories/WC%20Test%20Category` (by name instead of ID) --
  **422**, same `ValidationError`/"Id must be of type PydanticObjectId"
  shape as `GET /products/<sku>` in Phase 0. Only the Mongo ObjectId works
  as `{identifier}` on this resource too -- `API V3.md`'s identifier
  flexibility claim doesn't hold here either.
}
